%N A091283 Exponent of 2 in the prime factorization of prime(n)^4 - 1.
%C A091283 Also, exponent of 2 in -1+prime(n)^s if s is an exponent of the form 8*k-4 (previous definition). - _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 21 2026
%H A091283 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A091283/b091283.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A091283 From _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 21 2026: (Start)
%F A091283 a(n) = A007814(A030514(n)-1).
%F A091283 a(n) = A091282(n) + 1 for n >= 2.
%F A091283 Asymptotic mean: Limit_{m->oo} (1/m) * Sum_{k=1..m} a(k) = 5. (End)
%t A091283 IntegerExponent[Prime[Range[105]]^4 - 1, 2] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 21 2026 *)
%o A091283 (PARI) a(n) = valuation(prime(n)^4-1, 2); \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 21 2026
